[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. The reports merged into it
describe three problems. The queued parser fix closes the first one only.

<Callout kind="warn">
Fixing the parser leaves two problems open: the booking-v3 date hint, and dates that move by one day.
Each now has a ticket of its own.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {filed} />

1. **`parser`, the shared parser reads dates month first** ([issue 1](https://github.com/ktolembek/what-it-shows/issues/1)).
   Every tenant on file writes the day first. Their dates come out with day and month swapped.
   This is what #4471 describes, and what its queued fix is for.
2. **`hint`, the booking-v3 form tells people to type month first** ([issue 2](https://github.com/ktolembek/what-it-shows/issues/2)).
   The form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type what it says, and the form reads
   the date day first. The parser is not involved, so the parser fix does not touch it. Only
   reports that came in through the form, from tenants on booking-v3.
3. **`one-day`, dates move by one day** ([issue 3](https://github.com/ktolembek/what-it-shows/issues/3)).
   These reports describe no swap: Tuesday becomes Monday, or two recipients see different days.
   That points at time zones or the day boundary, not at date order. The desk already listed them
   in `desk-notes.json`.

## Why they stayed merged

- **Intake tags guess from the browser.** `meta.intakeTag` comes from the reporter's browser locale,
  not from the tenant. It says `parser` for most hint reports and `hint` for some parser reports.
  The counts above come from the tenant's locale and booking form (`causes.ts`), not from the tag.
- **Subjects don't tell them apart.** The same subject lines turn up in all three problems,
  so matching on subject ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) cannot split them.
- **The old table counts one-day moves as `parser`.** On the #4471 page they are only a footnote,
  and the hint row says "no ticket of its own". Here is that table, unchanged:

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## For the desk

- Close each issue on its own fix. A queued parser fix does not close #4471's other two problems.
- New reports from booking-v3 form users go to issue 2, even when intake tags them `parser`.
- A report where the day moves by one goes to issue 3. Add its id to `oneDayMove` in
  `desk-notes.json`, and this page counts it.

